# Cursor Rules for Archaser Project

> **Note**: This project uses modular rules files in `.cursor/rules/` directory.
> See individual rule files for specific guidelines:
> - `.cursor/rules/critical-rules.mdc` - Critical rules and development workflow
> - `.cursor/rules/planning.mdc` - Impact analysis, plan generation, repo plan copies, and **required codebase scan before finalizing plans**
> - `.cursor/rules/testing.mdc` - Testing guidelines and test planning
> - `.cursor/rules/test-unit-creation-process.mdc` - Process for creating integration/e2e test units (cron/workflow flows)
> - `.cursor/rules/translations.mdc` - Internationalization (i18n) rules
> - `.cursor/rules/design-system.mdc` - Design system and styling guidelines
> - `.cursor/rules/database.mdc` - Database (Prisma) guidelines
> - `.cursor/rules/api.mdc` - API guidelines
> - `.cursor/rules/frontend.mdc` - Frontend guidelines

## Quick Reference

### Local issue tracker (`/to-issues`)

**`/to-issues` publishes vertical slices as markdown under `.scratch/`, not ClickUp.** See `docs/agents/issue-tracker.md` and `.agents/skills/to-issues/SKILL.md`.

| Key | Value |
|-----|-------|
| **Root** | `.scratch/<feature-slug>/` |
| **Issues** | `.scratch/<feature-slug>/issues/<NN>-<slug>.md` (from `01`) |
| **Overview (2+ slices)** | `.scratch/<feature-slug>/OVERVIEW.md` |
| **Default status** | `ready-for-agent` (see `docs/agents/triage-labels.md`) |

Do **not** call ClickUp MCP from `/to-issues`. ClickUp remains for ad-hoc tasks and human workflow outside this skill.

**How to test:** Every slice file must include a short **How to test** section (where to go, what to do, what to expect).

**After implementation:** When a session was scoped to a specific slice file and work is complete, update that slice’s `**Status:**` to `done` in the markdown file at the end of the same session (unless the user opted out or work is partial).

### ClickUp Integration

**Single source of truth** for skills that *do* create or update ClickUp tasks (ad-hoc features/bugs, human workflow) — do **not** duplicate these IDs in skill files. When the user overrides a value in chat, that override wins for the session. **Vertical slices use `/to-issues` → `.scratch/`, not ClickUp.**

#### Project config

| Key | Value |
|-----|-------|
| **MCP server** | `user-clickup` |
| **Workspace ID** | `25708732` |
| **Default space** | **ARchaser** — `90122374962` |
| **Default list** | **ARchaser** — `901206394222` |
| **Default status** | **Selected for Development** |
| **Default assignee** | **Nilotpal Bose** — `93674717` (`nilotpal@archaser.com`) |

Pass `workspace_id` on hierarchy/search calls unless the user specifies another team. Create new tasks in the **default list** unless the user specifies another list.

Do not use other spaces in the same workspace (e.g. Development, Zman App) unless explicitly requested. Use `clickup_get_workspace_hierarchy` or `clickup_get_list` only when the user directs a different list.

**Creating tasks:** When creating a ClickUp task (feature or bug), **always** add a short **How to test** paragraph in the task description (`markdown_description` preferred). Include concrete steps: where to go in the app, what to do, and what to expect. For bugs, include steps to reproduce and to verify the fix. Do not create tasks without this section unless the user explicitly opts out.

